   "question": "Looking back over your life so far, when was the most going on for you, and about what years?",
   "words": "Gran Hazel dying, when I was 22, is the one I'd pick. That winter I barely slept, I lost the bookshop job by spring, and I stopped calling Mum back until the garden centre took me on in November. People say Callum going north was hard on the house too, but I was away at college then and only heard about it on the phone."
